1. Accept Only Https traffic 
	* Changes re in Prod_ProjectSecurityConfig.java
	*  http.requiresChannel(rcc->rcc.anyRequest().requiresSecure()); // Allows only https calls - redirects to 8443[default port of https]
	* http.requiresChannel(rcc->rcc.anyRequest().requiresInsecure()); // Allows only http calls
	
2. Exception Handling in Spring Security Framework
	* 401 - Authentication Exception, USe authentication failed.  - AuthenticationException
	* 403 - Forbidden Exception - User is authenticated , but dont have access to a specific API/resource. AccessDeniedException.
	* Spring security handles only these 2 exceptions 
	
3. SessionTimeout & Invalid Session configuration
	* By Default the cookie is generated as JSESSIONId, default timeout is 30 minute.
	* To modify this "server.servlet.session.timeout=20m" in application.yml, time out should be greater than 2min always.
	* In ProjectSecurityConfig.java -> http.sessionManagement(smc->smc.invalidSessionUrl("/invalidSession")); // Once time out redirect to this page 
	
4. Concurrent Sessions
	*  In ProjectSecurityConfig.java -> http.sessionManagement(smc->smc.invalidSessionUrl("/invalidSession")// Once time out redirect to this page
												.maximumSessions(1)  // Maximum Sessions a user can have. This will invalidate the previous session and new session is cretaed. To avoid this we use below
												.maxSessionsPreventsLogin(true)); // This wont allow for second session to be created till the 1st session is timedout or expired.
												
